In article <3A9C1772.D37E719@digitaldune.net>, "Dennis J. Sylvester" <dsylvester@digitaldune.net> writes:

>4.x and 5.x are not binary compatible.

While this may or may not be true for the specific library, it
isn't true in the general case.  There are plenty of programs
compiled on V4 and earlier that will to work fine on V5.  I
have programs compiled on V1.3A that still work on V5.1.  I
also have programs (Monitor) that do require complication and
sometimes code changes between versions.

It really depends on what the program does and how much it
depends on undocumented or moderately unstable interfaces.

