Having done a full installation of Tru64 5.0A on a single Alphaserver DS20E a
while ago, I'm slowly coming to terms with seeing those ugly-looking
context-dependent symbolic links (CDSL) everywhere. Things like...

  syslog.conf -> ../cluster/members/{memb}/etc/syslog.conf

Can anyone confirm that this is all as expected for a standalone install? The
System Administration manual on the Documentation CD says in Section 6.2

  "The root (/), /var, and /usr file systems each have a /cluster
  subdirectory that is not used on a single system, but must not be deleted
  or the system cannot be added into a cluster at some future time."
  
But, to me, it looks like the cluster directories *are* used on a *single*
system - otherwise the symbolic links like that above wouldn't point to
anything?

Of Tru64 installed systems, I wonder what percentage are in real clusters?

-- 
