There are two paths for upgrading:

1> 4.0[DF] -> 4.0G -> 5.1

4.0G is nothing more than 4.0F for WildFire; it is a hardware 'upgrade'
only.  However, even though you can go from 4.0F to 5.1 it is not
'officially' supported by Compaq and if you get into trouble your screwed.
Therefore, to stay 'official'  upgrade from D or F to G, and then when you
are ready for 5.1 it is a direct upgrade with minimal headaches.

2> 4.0F -> 5.0a -> 5.1

I this case, since Compaq does not support 4.0F to 5.1 direct upgrade you
have to take the intermediate step with 5.0a.  This is not painless,
requires a lot of work to 5.0a, and the chances are high, if you are not
well versed in Tru64, you can screw yourself.

The move to 5.1 is a large leap (it is also sizable for 5.0a) since the
entire underlying structure of the OS is changing and WILL break your
applications if you do not plan properly.  Unless you are clustering systems
and require 5.1 with TruCluster 5.1 don't waste your time.  5.1 is
outstanding, but you really need to weigh the reasons you are choosing  it.

I have performed the various upgrade paths on hundreds of systems from
2100's to ES40's and maintain the 5.1 on systems as large as GS80's
(looser's), GS160's and GS320's with fully loaded QBB's.

Dennis.  -Tru64 is cool because it's different.  It takes a real SA to
handle it!

