I also don't have a deap understanding of how it works, but I would discribe it
that way:

The major number indicates the device driver while the minor number indicates
the location (Bus, Target, Lun) of the device. Now you may be confused because
one would think that the minor number is related to a phisical location. But it
isn't like that anymore in V5.x. It only points to a hardwaredb where the
information about the phisical location of the drive. This basicaly means, that
you can change the drive location and preserve the major/minor number. In most
cases this isn't needed, but in some cases it may be... (advfs for example
doesn't care about that and I don't know an example that does).

I never had problems using dsfmgr, but anyway: the right way to replace a disk
is hwmgr.

Hope that helps for the understanding... Cheers, Igor



