I always look at upgrade paths when researching systems.  What you need
today may be too small tomorrow.  The GS80 requires an entire frame roll to
upgrade to a GS160.  A better option is to start with a 160 with fewer CPU's
and ower memory.  Then you can add CPU's and memory as needed. When you top
out, you just add a frame and become a 320.  Then you can continue to expand
the 320 as needed.

Personal preference and opinion.

Dennis.

