I used an OEM hard disk once, and it seemed to work at first.
Then I upgraded the OS, and the machine started crashing
every few weeks under load.
The OEM couldn't help. By chance I found out that it
was caused by insufficient SCSI tagged queuing depth.
It now *seems to be* running fine as a non-system disk
with a custom entry in the hard disk configuration file.
I could have saved the learning experience if I'd
used a disk that had been tested with that system.

