I think you need to define what you mean by a cluster here otherwise
people may get confused as to what it is you are trying to do! 

If you mean 8 nodes with a fast interconnect for running MPI then it's
probably not a good idea to call it a cluster on this list :-)  These
days on Tru64 the term cluster implies a lot more than just a fast
message passing interconect, it means a cluster wide filesystem that
isn't NFS, distributed services, lock managers, fail over and a host of
other functionality. To run it you need either Memory Channel or an SC
system with a QSW switch. 

I doubt Myrinet can be used to provide Trucluster functionality but if
you mean 8 nodes with myrinet in a Beowulf style setup then that is
something completly different.

Nick Hill
