SC Zhong schrieb:
> 
> I wish to build a 8 nodes cluster with DS20E,
> using the compaq solution of memory channel is
> easier but expensive.  I am thinking about
> using myrinet, could you share some experiences
> in terms of maintainability, performance with me
> if you have built such a cluster?  I plan to
> use the cluster to run some fortran codes parallelizing
> under MPI.
> thanks in advance
> 
Hi,

we use a 16 node Myrinet cluster. We don't have any cluster management
software to install software, patches etc., but you may want to test
Compaq CMU. 
We don't use the MCP, GM and MPICH software from Myri, but we use
ParaStation2 (see http://www.par-tec.com). There are some advantages of
the ParaStation software in functionality, maintainability and
availability; you should browse ParTec's web pages for them (the pages
aren't updated very often, if you want up-to-date information, you have
to send them your questions by E-mail). There are some benchmark results
on these pages, too. The drawback is, that you get Myri's software for
free, but you have to pay for ParaStation.
Our cluster works very well (we use MPI and C, C++ and Fortran), and
here in Germany 16 rackmounted XP1000/667MHz/768MB with Myri hardware
and ParaStation software are less than half the price of a
GS160/731Mhz/8GB.
Don't forget a batch queueing system for your cluster, a good starting
point is http://www.csse.monash.edu.au/~jon/bqs.html.

HTH and regards,
Ralf Eichmann


