Hallo Jo�p!

 JRG> Which kernel parameters should I change in order to run the 
 JRG> query without memory problems.

You shoudl set "ulimit -d unlimited" and "ulimit -m unlimited" before 
running the program that queries large amounts of memory. You must run 
this in the same shell where the program is started, i.E. write a shell 
script that first runs these and then runs the program.

Also note that due to the virtual memory strategy of Tru64, you need at 
least the same amount of swap space as you have memory installed, 
better twice that amount. Even if the swap space will not be used at 
all, you need it in order to be able to allocate the full amount of 
your physical memory. Tru64 wants to be sure it can always swap out 
everything if need should be.

Viele Gr��e,
Tobias



