Thank you, I have resolved this issue now.  
Incase you're curious, here's what it was:

I updated the firmware, and it had no effect.  In most of the 
documentation, it simply said "The driver for the KGPSA is built into Tru64  
4.0 and greater and is supported by the console driver."  However, in 
looking around and digging deeper, there was one document that said I need 
NHD2 or NHD3 or Patch Kit 2 (BL13) or Patch Kit 3.
At the tru64 web page, I was able to download Patch Kit 4 (the older 
versions aren't available anymore).  The installation was amazingly slick.  
Afterward, when I performed the genvmunix boot and kernel build, the driver 
was indeed fixed.

The next problem I ran into was:  No Cluster FS.  I had about a bazillion 
disks appear under /dev, because of the multiple paths to reach the same 
disk.  Eventually straightened that out too.

