Officially speaking, the "A" series were only able to run NT and
the "AU" series could run Tru64 and OpenVMS. However, depending on the
internal components, many of the "A" series could run Tru64 just fine
too. What you describe you have should work fine. The only thing you
didn't mention was your SCSI adapter and SCSI disks. You have to boot
Tru64 from a SCSI disk and if you have an Adaptec SCSI card, that is
NOT supported (QLogic is the usual supported SCSI card in the DPW
series under Tru64). Your IDE hard drive should be usable as a data
drive, but not to boot from.

Regards,
Jeff D

