I don't know for sure but I don't think so. The SRM console is provided by a
different set of
BIOS chips which in principle should not be present on the "a" series. The
firmware is the
microcode that runs on the SRM console hardware, not the hardware itself. You'd
need a
new motherboard.

Anyway, IF you do have SRM regardless of what I said above, there should be an
item
on one of the menus in your ARC console that says something like 'switch to
other OS'
you select that, power off, count to 10, power on, and you should now have an
SRM
console (black screen, >>> prompt).

Cheers,

Pedro.





