andy thomas wrote:
> 
> I've added an HP CD-RW drive to a PWS 500au but I don't know what the
> device name would be. It's on the SCSI bus - the exiting IDE CDROM is
> accessible via /dev/rz8c.
> 

As you quote /dev/rz8c as an existing device I am assuming you are on a
version of the OS prior to V5. In this case the device name is derived
from the SCSI bus it is connected to and the SCSI id of the drive on
that bus. The device number is Bus*8+deviceID. You may need to use
MAKEDEV to make the device or use perhaps 

scsimgr -scan_all

If the device file has been created then the file command can be used to
show what they all are:

file /dev/rrz*c

should show you


