> I ve a problem:
> after the cluster creation the ip address of the cluster alias and of the
> members are changed. How can i reconfigure the cluster ?
> 
> I've read the "best practice documentation" about how to change the ip of
> only one member. But how can i change all the ip in the cluster, cluster
> alias ip too ?
> 
> Thanks.. and i'm sorry for my poor english.

Following the procedure that I made with a two-member cluster with
TruCluster V5.0:
1) Change IP-Address in /etc/rc.config on each member.
2) If need be change your members and cluster alias in /etc/hosts
3) Look  for .member1.cfg (the file belonging to the leading cluster
member
   during cluster installation) in /cluster/admin: search for
clu_alias_ip 
   and change cluster alias as you wish
4) reboot the cluster
5) hope that works as it worked for me...

