I have seen this problem with ftp and telnet daemons. It can happen
because when you try to connect via telnet the telnet daemon does a
reverse DNS lookup (i.e. resolves an IP to a hostname) to try to get a
hostname for the telnet client. If the host on which the telnet daemon
is running can't resolve the IP to a hostname it eventually gives up.
The length of time it takes to give up could be causing your telnet
delay.

The solution is to either:

- Turn off hostname resolution in your telnet daemon configuration. (I
don't know how to do this)

-OR-

- For each host from which you want to telnet to the Tru64 box from, put
an entry in /etc/hosts for that host.

If you look in your Tru64's /etc/hosts you'll probably find an entry for
your AIX box - that's why the login prompt is instant.

Hope this helps,

Ben.

