Jouk Jansen <joukj@hrem.stm.tudelft.nl> writes:
> Is it a known problem that c++(gcc) cannot include gethostbyname?

Works here.  Some version numbers might be helpful.

> focus-jj) c++ test.cpp
> /usr/ucb/ld:
> Unresolved:
> gethostbyname(char const *)
> collect2: ld returned 1 exit status

There's a hint there.  Consider the program

extern void nosuchCC(char const*);
extern "C" void nosuchc(char const*);

main()
{
   nosuchCC("asdf");
   nosuchc("asdf");
}

Try compiling it with c++ -- you should see something like

dsr_lns130% g++ asdf.cc 
/usr/bin/ld:
Unresolved:
nosuchCC(char const *)
nosuchc
collect2: ld returned 1 exit status

Now look back at your error message -- "gethostbyname(char const *)"
means it saw a prototype, but saw it in a C++ context, so it is
looking for a C++ mangled name.  <netdb.h> is supposed to take care
of this via 

_BEGIN_CPLUSPLUS
_END_CPLUSPLUS

lines that are translated into

extern "C" {
}

if __cplusplus is defined (all this in <standards.h>).  Your error
means that for some reason this isn't happening.  A 'c++ -E test.cpp'
to see what the preprocessor is doing might be enlightening.
-- 
