Not that I would be an Unix person, but does it really
matter...
840KB/s may be reasonable performance if you have 10Mbit/s
adapter connector to 10Mbit/s network. If the other Alpha
however has 100Mbit/s adapter connected to same 10Mbit/s
network then also 34KB/s performance is to be expected
and therefore reasonable.

On the other hand, if the network and adapters are really
100Mbit/s on both machines, then I would not necessarily
call 840KB/s a reasonable performance...

Which way do you have it? If 10Mbit/s network, then try
setting EWA0_MODE to TWISTED_PAIR, i.e. lowering the 5.1
Alpha to 10Mbit/s HALF DUPLEX mode.

_veli

